ase":"H5857","lemma":"עַי","tr":"ay","gloss":"Ai","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":40},{"base":"H3412","lemma":"יַרְמוּת","tr":"yar·mut","gloss":"Jarmuth","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"H5700","lemma":"עֶגְלוֹן","tr":"eg·lon","gloss":"Eglon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":13},{"base":"H5927","lemma":"עָלָה","tr":"a·lah","gloss":"to ascend: rise","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":889},{"base":"H3923","lemma":"לָכִישׁ","tr":"la·khish","gloss":"Lachish","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":24},{"base":"H1537","lemma":"גִּלְגָּל","tr":"gil·gal","gloss":"Gilgal","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":40},{"base":"H3389","lemma":"יְרוּשָׁלִַ֫ם, יְרוּשְׁלֵם","tr":"ye·ru·sha·laim","gloss":"Jerusalem","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":643}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":11,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"No man will be able to stand against you; the LORD your God will put the fear and dread of you upon all the land, wherever you set foot, as He has promised you.","from":2},{"book":"JOS","chapter":9,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And Joshua made a treaty of peace with them to let them live, and the leaders of the congregation swore an oath to them.","from":4},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Melchizedek king of Salem brought out bread and wine—since he was priest of God Most High—","from":1},{"book":"GEN","chapter":15,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"In the fourth generation your descendants will return here, for the iniquity of the Amorites is not yet complete.”","from":5},{"book":"GEN","chapter":23,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"She died in Kiriath-arba (that is, Hebron) in the land of Canaan, and Abraham went out to mourn and to weep for her.","from":3},{"book":"GEN","chapter":37,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then Israel told him, “Go now and see how your brothers and the flocks are faring, and bring word back to me.” So he sent him off from the Valley of Hebron. And when Joseph arrived in Shechem,","from":3},{"book":"EXO","chapter":15,"verse":14,"verseEnd":16,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The nations will hear and tremble; anguish will grip the dwellers of Philistia. Then the chiefs of Edom will be dismayed; trembling will seize the leaders of Moab; those who dwell in Canaan will melt away, and terror and dread will fall on them. By the power of Your arm they will be as still as a stone until Your people pass by, O LORD, until the people You have bought pass by.","from":2},{"book":"NUM","chapter":13,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"They went up through the Negev and came to Hebron, where Ahiman, Sheshai, and Talmai, the descendants of Anak, dwelled. It had been built seven years before Zoan in Egypt.","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"8-15":{"people":[{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":4,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":5,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"amorites-h0567","name":"Amorites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanites","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"jashar-h3477h","name":"Jashar","kind":"person","brief":"Author of book","count":1,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"gilgal-h1537g","name":"Gilgal","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"azekah-h5825","name":"Azekah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"beth-horon-lower-h1032i","name":"Beth-horon Lower","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"gibeon-h1391","name":"Gibeon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"makkedah-h4719","name":"Makkedah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"aijalon-h0357","name":"Aijalon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12}],"words":[{"base":"H1032","lemma":"בֵּית חוֹרֹן","tr":"bet cho·ron","gloss":"Beth-horon","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":28},{"base":"H3091","lemma":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","tr":"ye·ho·shu·a","gloss":"Joshua","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":218},{"base":"H8121","lemma":"שֶׁ֫מֶשׁ","tr":"she·mesh","gloss":"sun","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":134},{"base":"H5825","lemma":"עֲזֵקָה","tr":"a·ze·qah","gloss":"Azekah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"H3394","lemma":"יָרֵחַ","tr":"ya·re·ach","gloss":"moon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":27},{"base":"H1826","lemma":"דָּמַם","tr":"da·mam","gloss":"to silence: stationary","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":30},{"base":"H1391","lemma":"גִּבְעוֹן","tr":"giv·on","gloss":"Gibeon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":37},{"base":"H1537","lemma":"גִּלְגָּל","tr":"gil·gal","gloss":"Gilgal","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":40},{"base":"H5975","lemma":"עָמַד","tr":"a·mad","gloss":"to stand: stand","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":521},{"base":"H0068","lemma":"אֶ֫בֶן","tr":"e·ven","gloss":"stone","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":273}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"HAB","chapter":3,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"Sun and moon stood still in their places at the flash of Your flying arrows, at the brightness of Your shining spear.","from":12},{"book":"ISA","chapter":38,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"I will make the sunʼs shadow that falls on the stairway of Ahaz go back ten steps.’” So the sunlight went back the ten steps it had descended.","from":12},{"book":"HAB","chapter":3,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"Sun and moon stood still in their places at the flash of Your flying arrows, at the brightness of Your shining spear.","from":13},{"book":"DEU","chapter":1,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"The LORD your God, who goes before you, will fight for you, just as you saw Him do for you in Egypt","from":14},{"book":"ISA","chapter":38,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"I will make the sunʼs shadow that falls on the stairway of Ahaz go back ten steps.’” So the sunlight went back the ten steps it had descended.","from":13},{"book":"EXO","chapter":14,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD will fight for you; you need only to be still.”","from":14},{"book":"ROM","chapter":8,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"What then shall we say in response to these things? If God is for us, who can be against us?","from":8},{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"But the LORD said to me, “Do not fear him, for I have delivered him into your hand, along with all his people and his land. Do to him as you did to Sihon king of the Amorites, who lived in Heshbon.”","from":8}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"16-28":{"people":[{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":10,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":20}],"places":[{"id":"makkedah-h4719","name":"Makkedah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":4,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"eglon-h5700g","name":"Eglon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"hebron-h2275a","name":"Hebron","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"jarmuth-h3412g","name":"Jarmuth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"lachish-h3923","name":"Lachish","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"jericho-h3405g","name":"Jericho","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":28}],"words":[{"base":"H3091","lemma":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","tr":"ye·ho·shu·a","gloss":"Joshua","lang":"h","inPassage":11,"uses":218},{"base":"H4631","lemma":"מְעָרָה","tr":"me·a·rah","gloss":"cave","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":39},{"base":"H4719","lemma":"מַקֵּדָה","tr":"maq·qe·dah","gloss":"Makkedah","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":9},{"base":"H2568","lemma":"חָמֵשׁ","tr":"cha·mesh","gloss":"five","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":343},{"base":"H2244","lemma":"חָבָא","tr":"cha·va","gloss":"to hide","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":33},{"base":"H0428","lemma":"אֵ֫לֶּה","tr":"el·leh","gloss":"these","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":746},{"base":"H6310","lemma":"פֶּה","tr":"peh","gloss":"lip","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":498},{"base":"H0408","lemma":"אַל","tr":"al","gloss":"not","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":724},{"base":"H6086","lemma":"עֵץ","tr":"ets","gloss":"tree: wood","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":330},{"base":"H8518","lemma":"תָּלָה","tr":"ta·lah","gloss":"to hang","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":27}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":1,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Have I not commanded you to be strong and courageous? Do not be afraid; do not be discouraged, for the LORD your God is with you wherever you go.”","from":25},{"book":"2CO","chapter":1,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"He has delivered us from such a deadly peril, and He will deliver us. In Him we have placed our hope that He will yet again deliver us,","from":25},{"book":"DEU","chapter":7,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"the great trials that you saw, the signs and wonders, and the mighty hand and outstretched arm by which the LORD your God brought you out. The LORD your God will do the same to all the peoples you now fear.","from":25},{"book":"DEU","chapter":31,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Be strong and courageous; do not be afraid or terrified of them, for it is the LORD your God who goes with you; He will never leave you nor forsake you.”","from":25},{"book":"DEU","chapter":31,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD Himself goes before you; He will be with you. He will never leave you nor forsake you. Do not be afraid or discouraged.”","from":25},{"book":"1SA","chapter":17,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"David added, “The LORD, who delivered me from the claws of the lion and the bear, will deliver me from the hand of this Philistine.” “Go,” said Saul, “and may the LORD be with you.”","from":25},{"book":"ROM","chapter":8,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"No, in all these things we are more than conquerors through Him who loved us.","from":25},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Finally, be strong in the Lord and in His mighty power.","from":25}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"29-43":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":10,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":10,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"horam-h2036","name":"Horam","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":33}],"places":[{"id":"libnah-h3841h","name":"Libnah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":4,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"makkedah-h4719","name":"Makkedah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29},{"id":"jericho-h3405g","name":"Jericho","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":30},{"id":"lachish-h3923","name":"Lachish","kind":"place","brief":"","count":5,"firstVerse":31},{"id":"gezer-h1507","name":"Gezer","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"eglon-h5700g","name":"Eglon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":3,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"hebron-h2275a","name":"Hebron","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"debir-h1688a","name":"Debir","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":38},{"id":"negeb-h5045g","name":"Negeb","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":40},{"id":"shephelah-h8219","name":"Shephelah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":40},{"id":"gaza-h5804","name":"Gaza","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":41},{"id":"gibeon-h1391","name":"Gibeon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":41},{"id":"goshen-h1657h","name":"Goshen","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":41},{"id":"kadesh-h6946g","name":"Kadesh","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":41},{"id":"gilgal-h1537g","name":"Gilgal","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":43}],"words":[{"base":"H3091","lemma":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","tr":"ye·ho·shu·a","gloss":"Joshua","lang":"h","inPassage":10,"uses":218},{"base":"H3841","lemma":"לִבְנָה","tr":"liv·nah","gloss":"Libnah","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":18},{"base":"H3923","lemma":"לָכִישׁ","tr":"la·khish","gloss":"Lachish","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":24},{"base":"H9034","lemma":"הָ","tr":"ha","gloss":"her","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":490},{"base":"H8300","lemma":"שָׂרִיד","tr":"sa·rid","gloss":"survivor","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":28},{"base":"H5221","lemma":"נָכָה","tr":"na·khah","gloss":"to smite","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":500},{"base":"H3898","lemma":"לָחַם","tr":"la·cham","gloss":"to fight","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":177},{"base":"H3920","lemma":"לָכַד","tr":"la·khad","gloss":"to capture","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":121},{"base":"H7604","lemma":"שָׁאַר","tr":"sha·ar","gloss":"to remain","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":133},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":1051}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"There has been no day like it before or since, when the LORD listened to the voice of a man, because the LORD fought for Israel.","from":42},{"book":"JOS","chapter":11,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So Joshua took this entire region: the hill country, all the Negev, all the land of Goshen, the western foothills, the Arabah, and the mountains of Israel and their foothills,","from":41},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"From there he marched against the inhabitants of Debir (formerly known as Kiriath-sepher).","from":38},{"book":"JOS","chapter":16,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But they did not drive out the Canaanites who lived in Gezer. So the Canaanites dwell among the Ephraimites to this day, but they are forced laborers.","from":33},{"book":"JDG","chapter":1,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Judah also marched against the Canaanites who were living in Hebron (formerly known as Kiriath-arba), and they struck down Sheshai, Ahiman, and Talmai.","from":36},{"book":"JDG","chapter":1,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Ephraim also failed to drive out the Canaanites living in Gezer; so the Canaanites continued to dwell among them in Gezer.","from":33},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and the borders of Canaan extended from Sidon toward Gerar as far as Gaza, and then toward Sodom, Gomorrah, Admah, and Zeboiim, as far as Lasha.","from":41},{"book":"GEN","chapter":13,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"So Abram moved his tent and went to live near the Oaks of Mamre at Hebron, where he built an altar to the Lord.","from":36}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}